  body: `Prior Lessons — 1-Sentence Recap

Lesson 016: Wafer-start capacity becomes useful only after translating it through utilization, die size, yield and downstream constraints.

Lesson 017: Large dies suffer fewer candidates per wafer and greater defect exposure, making yield especially important for AI accelerators.

Lesson 018: Masks and reticles carry lithography's master patterns, while the reticle field limits the size of a conventional monolithic die.

Lesson 019: Photoresist converts the scanner's optical image into a temporary physical stencil that later processes can act on.

